From: XR1710G Community <xr1710g-community@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: evaluate HIT_UNBIND packets for bridge offload

The XR1710G mesh repeater datapath can remain in PPE UNBIND state without
raising HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED. In that state airoha_ppe_check_skb() is
never called, so the bridge fallback cannot resolve the learned FDB path to
an mt7996 WDMA/NPU egress and no BND entry is ever installed.

Runtime tracing on the XR1710G showed active bridge FDB, HWMP and MPP
entries while drv_net_fill_forward_path was never called and the PPE bind
table stayed empty. This means the offload preparation code was not reached,
rather than the mesh route lookup failing.

Evaluate normal HIT_UNBIND packets as well as HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED.
Once a flow is successfully bound the PPE reason changes and this path is no
longer taken. Unbindable traffic continues on the normal software path.

---
 include/linux/soc/airoha/airoha_offload.h | 1 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c   | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/linux/soc/airoha/airoha_offload.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/airoha/airoha_offload.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
 enum {
+	PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND = 0x0e,
 	PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED = 0x0f,
 };
 
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -646,7 +646,8 @@ static int airoha_qdma_rx_process(struct
 				     PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
 
 		reason = FIELD_GET(AIROHA_RXD4_PPE_CPU_REASON, msg1);
-		if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED)
+		if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND ||
+		    reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED)
 			airoha_ppe_check_skb(&eth->ppe->dev, q->skb, hash,
 					     false);
 
-- 
